# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore - Computer Vision Project
# ==============================================================================
# WHAT GOES TO GIT VS WHAT GOES TO GOOGLE DRIVE:
#
# Track in Git (Submit to Repository):
#   - Source code (src/*.py, main.py)
#   - Project documentation (README.md, requirements.txt, .gitignore)
#   - Input instructions (inputs/README.md)
#   - Report templates & outlines (report/*.md)
#   - Directory placeholders (.gitkeep)
#
# DO NOT Track in Git (Upload to Google Drive / Keep Local):
#   - Personal raw photos and videos (inputs/photo_original.jpg, etc.)
#   - Large video files (*.mp4, *.avi, *.mov)
#   - Deep learning model weights (*.pt, *.pth, *.onnx, yolov8n.pt)
#   - Heavy generated outputs (*.png, *.jpg, *.csv, *.json)
# ==============================================================================

# Python bytecode and cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# IDE & Editor settings
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Operating system files
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# User-provided personal media in inputs/ (preserve inputs/README.md)
inputs/*.jpg
inputs/*.jpeg
inputs/*.png
inputs/*.mp4
inputs/*.mov
inputs/*.avi
inputs/*.mkv
inputs/*.webm

# Pretrained deep learning model weights
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.weights
*.bin
yolov8*.pt
yolo11*.pt

# Generated outputs (preserve folder structure via .gitkeep)
outputs/**/*
!outputs/**/.gitkeep
!outputs/.gitkeep
